      "side": 1,
      "message": "The OutputFileProducer is not used by deapexer. It did not work. Hence why I added DeapexerInfo. I kept the same tag concept though. There is room for improvements and clarity there. e.g. Instead of using a separate tag it could just use the APEX relative path, e.g. instead of `core-libart{.dexjar}` it could use javalib/core-libart.jar.\n\nYour understanding of how and why the information is passed back and forth is broadly correct.\n\nWhat the BCPF and java prebuilt modules pass to deapexer (indirectly) is a map from ID to a string path of a file in the APEX, e.g. core-libart{.dexjar}-\u003ejavalib/core-libart.jar, what it gets back is a map from the same ID to an android.Path of a file in the file system, e.g. core-libart{.dexjar}-\u003eout/soong/.....deapexer.../javalib/core-libart.jar.\n\nThe part that the prebuilt_apex does not know is the \"out/soong/.....deapexer...\" path. We could avoid using maps at all and just make that path available in DeapexerInfo and then have PrebuiltExportPath() just prepend that. However, I think a map of exported files is safer as it allows Soong to detect an attempt to use a file that is not exported.\n\nWill look at simplifying all of this in a follow up CL.",
